# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# REVIEW c953b22: under --walk-methods a callable-merge host the knob does not walk stays native
# (its return and its calls of the model are built there), and l2trans says so in a note, located:
# here its declaration `size_t: big (n)` needs a conversion, whose receiver can throw, and a
# throwing method stays native -- "l2trans note: ...: the callable merge host makeAdder stays
# native under --walk-methods: it can throw".  The program runs natively: add5(1) = 6.  Mutant: no
# note -- the row's Notes line is missing.  Entry 7.
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    size_t: big (n)
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: n + x
    return: addN

@: add5 makeAdder(5)
int: a (add5: 1)
int: ok 0
if: a = 6
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
